conversation.reasoning_content:
Two errors:
1. Partial move of `self.state` in the timeout match, then `self.fail_with` borrows self. The issue: `self.state = match (self.state, pending) { ... }` — the tuple `(self.state, pending)` moves self.state (the whole State). Then in the ping arm, `self.fail_with(...)` borrows self mutably while... the moved `self.state` is in the tuple being matched. Since the match scrutinee `(self.state, pending)` is an owned tuple, moving out of `self.state` results in a partial move of self, and then `self.fail_with` needs `&mut self` — the compiler rejects because part of self was moved.

Fix: match on `pending` only (not self.state), since we know state is AwaitingResponse here:

```rust
let pending = self.pending_request.take();
self.state = match pending {
    Some(PendingRequest::Single(Request::Ping(_), _)) => {
        self.fail_with(PeerError::ClientRequestTimeout);
        State::Failed
    }
    Some(pending) => {
        let e = PeerError::ClientRequestTimeout;
        let tx = match pending {
            PendingRequest::Single(_, tx) | PendingRequest::BlocksByHash { tx, .. } => tx,
        };
        let _ = tx.send(Err(Arc::new(e).into()));
        State::AwaitingRequest
    }
    None => panic!("unreachable"),
};
```

This avoids moving self.state. Good.

2. handshake.rs constructs `Connection { ... }` without `pending_request`. Need to add `pending_request: None` there. Let me look at handshake.rs around line 198.

Also a warning: `mut block_requests` unused mut (I only read `.len()`). Remove `mut` from block_requests binding.

